.TH KEYRING-CRYPT 2
.SH NAME
keyring: aessetup, aescbc \- data encryption
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "keyring.m";
keyring := load Keyring Keyring->PATH;

Encrypt:   con 0;
Decrypt:   con 1;

AESbsize:  con 16;

aessetup:  fn(key: array of byte, ivec: array of byte): ref AESstate;
aescbc:    fn(state: ref AESstate, buf: array of byte,
             n: int, direction: int);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
These functions encrypt and decrypt blocks of data with AES
in cipher block chaining mode.
.PP
.B Aessetup
is given a secret
.I key
and an initialisation vector
.IR ivec ,
and returns an adt that holds the state of one encryption.
A sequence of blocks of data can then be encrypted or decrypted by repeatedly calling
.BR aescbc .
On each call,
.I buf
provides
.I n
bytes of the data to encrypt or decrypt.
.I N
need not be a multiple of the block size
.BR AESbsize ,
but then
for successful decryption, the decryptor must use the same
sequence of buffer sizes as the encryptor.
.I Direction
is the constant
.B Encrypt
or
.B Decrypt
as required.
.I State
maintains the encryption state, initially produced by
.BR aessetup ,
and updated as each buffer is encrypted or decrypted.
It is cleared when its last reference goes.
.PP
The algorithm is the Advanced Encryption Standard, AES (also known as Rijndael).
The
.I key
should be 16, 24 or 32 bytes long (128, 192 or 256 bits).
.I Ivec
should be
.B AESbsize
bytes of random data: random enough to be unlikely to be reused but
not cryptographically strongly unpredictable.
The cipher takes the same time whatever the key and the data
(it uses the processor's AES instructions where there are any,
and otherwise indexes no table by them);
without the instructions that costs speed, most of all in
.BR aescbc 's
encryption.
.PP
Cipher block chaining gives secrecy and no integrity: data that must
not be changed unseen is encrypted with one of Keyring's authenticated
ciphers instead
.RB ( aesgcmencrypt
or
.B ccpolyencrypt
in
.BR keyring.m ).
.PP
The DES, IDEA and Blowfish functions that were here are gone.
The DES ones had only raised an error for some time;
nothing in the system used the others but the
.B idea
command, which went with them.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR keyring-intro (2),
.IR keyring-rc4 (2),
.IR security-random (2)
